WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.920
Stand up straight and look me in the eye,
new recruits!

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.770
Now you listen up and you listen good, if
you’re watching this then that means you’ve

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.220
been selected to join the dedicated staff
of the SCP Foundation.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.250
Tell me, soldier, do you intend to give your
life in the service of the cause, and strive

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:20.150
to secure anomalies of all kinds, contain
those anomalies, and protect the innocent

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.749
general public from their influence or knowledge?

00:00:22.749 --> 00:00:24.579
That’s what I like to hear!

00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:28.840
Here at the Foundation, we have collected
some of the deadliest, most sophisticated,

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.310
and strangest weaponry the world has ever
seen.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.730
Forget everything you think you know about
combat, because I’m taking all of you back

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.730
to school.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.019
Sharpen your pencils and get ready to take
some detailed notes, because I’ll be taking

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:45.230
you into the Foundation Armory for a first-hand
look at some of the most powerful and anomalous

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.460
weaponry we have come across in our years
of operation.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:53.329
We try to avoid using any of these specimens
for combat purposes, but in this line of work,

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:57.350
you never know when you might need to be ready
to head into battle against any government,

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.860
an alien species, or evil itself.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.879
So our motto is, what?

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:04.379
Always be prepared for the worst!

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:08.660
Besides, one of these little peashooters might
wind up being the key to eventually neutralizing

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.520
SCP-682.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.520
Infernal lizard.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.520
Ahem.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.390
Anyway, let’s get down to business.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.340
Let’s start with the big guns.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.600
Meet SCP-044, secretly manufactured by German
engineers toward the during the Second World

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.600
War.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.790
044 is a howitzer, a large ranged weapon similar
to a cannon.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.090
If you’re intimidated by its size, you should
be.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:36.030
It’s 251 metric tons of artillery power,
and its unusual qualities keep going.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:42.350
Unlike other howitzers, which use a breech
for loading shells, 044 uses a giant air-compression

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.409
chamber.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:48.280
Any object that can fit into the weapon’s
muzzle can be used as ammunition.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.710
Once an object has been loaded in, the howitzer
somehow weakens its molecular and atomic bonds,

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.850
transforming it for ideal impact.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:01.870
Once the weapon is fired, the matter in the
barrel is shot out at high speed in the form

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.549
of a glowing red slug - slug as in projectile,
not the animal.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:09.970
Get it together, recruit - equal to the mass
of the original object loaded into the barrel.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:16.530
The largest slug produced so far was 19,500
pounds, the result of loading The Administrator’s

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.940
pickup truck into the muzzle of SCP-044.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.650
Up next, a weapon that packs a real bite.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:26.610
I don’t normally stoop to puns, but a sense
of humor is required to keep up morale around

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.910
here, so yes.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.960
That was a play on words.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.050
Don’t get used to it.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:38.830
SCP-127 appears to be an ordinary MP5K-PDW
submachine gun, with one notable exception:

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.020
it’s alive.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.470
Aside from its outer shell of steel and polymer,
tests have indicated that it is made of living,

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:46.470
organic material.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.390
When fired, the gun does not expel bullets,
but teeth.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:53.890
They look like human teeth, but DNA tests
found no match for any species on Earth.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:59.340
127 features semi-automatic and fully automatic
settings, and produces an audible groaning

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.750
sound when it switches between the two.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:06.030
So far, it doesn’t seem to be deadlier than
an ordinary weapon of the same type, but never

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:10.849
underestimate the importance of psychological
warfare or what it might do to an enemy soldier’s

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:15.569
thought process when he sees teeth flying
at him at lightning speed.

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:19.819
Up next we have, not a gun, but a blade.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:25.050
SCP-034 is a knife carved from pure obsidian,
with an estimated age of approximately 1000

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.050
years old.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:31.030
In all that time, it has not lost its edge,
and remains just as sharp as if it were freshly

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.030
made.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:35.900
But that’s not all: whoever wields this
knife is able to take on the appearance of

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.070
another person, as long as they have cut a
piece of their intended target’s skin off

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.489
with the knife.

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:45.080
It’s the ultimate tool for espionage.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.099
This next weapon may look like a toy, but
if you spend enough time at the Foundation

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:53.150
you’ll quickly learn that nothing is exactly
as it seems.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:58.700
SCP-3108 shares the appearance of a Nerf brand
dart gun, but this piece of machinery does

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:02.010
a lot more than shoot simple foam darts.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.299
Created by Nathan Pierce, this gun has the
ability to turn anything it hits into a worse

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:08.079
version of itself.

00:04:08.079 --> 00:04:12.620
A dollar turns into a quarter, a piece of
printer paper becomes one-ply toilet paper,

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:19.380
and - now here’s where its combat applications
come in - a human man turns into a neanderthal.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.990
Hit a man enough times with this Nerfing gun,
and he’ll degrade further and further each

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:28.090
time until he’s essentially just a tiny
earthworm you can crush beneath your boot.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:30.890
It’s nothing to play around with.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:36.700
Speaking of highly destructive weaponry that
looks like a toy, SCP-1068 is a collection

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.630
of model rockets, measuring at about a meter
in length apiece.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:46.970
On the back of their packaging, a note is
written: “Harness the Raw-ket power of Dr.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.090
Wondertainment's new line of model rockets
with The Atom Buster®!

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:57.500
This pint-sized monster launches a thousand
feet in the air before plummeting to a climactic

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.130
explosion of nuclear proportions.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.590
Truman would be proud.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:06.000
Utilizing a state-of-the-art light and sound
system, the greatest weapon ever detonated

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.600
can be used again… on your front lawn!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.230
You can even customize your model with the
accompanying realistic decal sheet to make

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.330
its launch a more awesome one.”

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:20.650
Though these pint-size rockets don’t pack
the punch of a real nuclear missile, they’re

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:25.510
more than capable of causing permanent damage
to the eyes and ears of anyone in the vicinity

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:29.500
when they’re detonated, as well as knocking
out all electronic communications in the area

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.070
for up to 20 hours.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:34.940
For a harmless-looking explosive that can
render an opponent blinded, deafened, and

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.790
unable to cry for help, these will do the
job just fine.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.850
Have you ever heard of the Bystander Effect?

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:44.430
It’s the concept that, when faced with a
horrific event, many people instinctively

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.220
will do nothing to stop it.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.690
Instead, they will simply stand by.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:54.210
SCP-668 weaponizes the Bystander Effect, and
guarantees it no matter what atrocities you

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.210
commit.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:59.520
It is a 13-inch chef’s knife with a rosewood
handle that, when held by a human being intending

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.970
to commit violence against another, gives
off a psychic signal that renders all nearby

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:07.060
sentient beings unable to intervene.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:11.110
Its effects have been reported as feeling
like an overwhelming sense of apathy.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:15.270
Additionally, it renders the victim of the
attack unable to defend themselves.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.270
There’s really no limit to the amount of
violence SCP-668’s holder could get away

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:24.330
with…but don’t get any ideas, this knife
is under high-level containment.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.580
Sometimes a weapon isn’t a blade, or a gun.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:31.490
Sometimes it’s a simple piece of plate glass,
like SCP-3154.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.980
I say simple, but you know the drill by now.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.010
It’s a bit more complicated than it looks.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:44.860
SCP-3154 is a triangular piece of glass, 16.2
cm long and 8 cm wide.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.810
When used to attack a person, the glass puts
them into an unusual state, referred to in

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:51.200
the official file as a Sigma State.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:57.050
And if I hear you making any “Sigma Male”
jokes during this presentation, mark my words,

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.950
I will snap your pencil-necks like stale breadsticks.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:06.400
A Sigma State is characterized by the following:
Absence of breathing and heartbeat, blood

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.830
settling in the lower parts of the body and
causing noticeable discoloration, gradual

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:15.020
reduction of body temperature, stiffness,
and a dramatically decreased immune system.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:20.610
If a person is left in a Sigma State for too
long, worms, flies, and other environmental

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.890
organisms will begin to feed on their body.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.710
Now, you might be wondering what’s so special
about this?

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.310
A Sigma State sounds like it’s just regular
old death.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.610
And you’re right, it is.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:34.650
This glass isn’t special because it kills
people, it’s special because it somehow

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:39.320
prevents anyone from recognizing its victims
as dead.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:43.930
Depending on who sees you use this piece of
glass to attack someone, you could quite literally

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.360
get away with murder.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:53.480
Up next is SCP-5175, a detailed knife with
a Moroccan style of design and an uncertain

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.480
origin.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.280
When handled by most people, this is nothing
more than a regular, if ornate, blade.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:05.470
However, when handled by the right person
- currently an individual known as PoI-3445

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:10.230
- the knife is able to remove any life form
from reality entirely.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:14.300
It doesn’t just kill them, it eradicates
them.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.810
Once the knife, in the hand of its designated
holder, has pierced a target, black mist begins

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.830
to pour from the target’s wound.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:25.530
It wraps around the target, and they disappear
completely, teleported out of our reality

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:31.310
and into an extradimensional space known as
“The Land of the Forsaken Suffering.”

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:35.680
The one who wields the knife is also accompanied
by the spirit of a Japanese samurai named

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.250
Kuroitanken Hanzo, a great warrior from the
1800s.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:44.460
It’s not just a knife capable of removing
its targets from this world, but it comes

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.800
with the experience of a long-dead veteran
fighter.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:52.010
SCP-958 also has a great deal of military
expertise to offer.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:58.140
It is a toy robot, made of plastic and tin,
standing at nineteen centimeters tall.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.980
On the bottom of the robot’s right foot,
there is text printed that reads: “General-Beep,

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:05.050
by Dr. Wondertainment.”

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:09.540
General-Beep is activated by flipping a switch
on the back of its head, at which point it

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.060
is able to speak and move on its own.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:16.800
When it is introduced to a child under the
age of 13, General-Beep will teach them about

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:22.300
military history, and will eventually teach
the child how to build copies of the toy robot,

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:26.510
as well as weapons including guns that shoot
paint, cannons that fire plush toys at high

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:32.130
speeds, and guns that shoot beams of focused
light hot enough to melt steel.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.990
It may be a toy, but this General is not playing
around.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:42.120
Up next, we have a set of anomalous hand grenades,
SCP-5969.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:47.130
These grenades are stored inside a World War
II-era wooden crate, and do not present any

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:53.580
unusual properties until they are exposed
to water in a liquid state, or to particularly

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.580
humid air.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:59.030
Once they have been exposed to enough moisture,
the grenades will instantly detonate, whether

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:02.400
the pin and spoon have been removed or not.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:08.820
While normal grenades expel metal shrapnel
on explosion, instances of SCP-5969 propel

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:13.380
seeds that sprout into flowering plants as
soon as they hit a solid surface.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:18.900
If these plants make contact with the skin
of a living person, they will begin to suck

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:23.670
out the person’s blood at a speed of 15
mL/second.

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:26.940
This will continue until the host has bled
to death.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:31.400
Really gives a new meaning to War of the Roses.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:37.030
SCP-5871 is not used for physical warfare,
but rather for metaphysical types of combat.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.880
It is an obsidian ritual knife with a gem-encrusted
handle.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:47.040
When the knife is used to symbolically kill
an entity via a specific, classified ritual,

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.900
it destroys that entity retroactively.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:56.810
This knife has been used to take care of multiple
dangerous intangible anomalies since its creation,

00:10:56.810 --> 00:11:00.140
and it is ready to be used again if the need
arises.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:04.670
Here we have SCP-4282, also known as Mutiny’s
Bane.

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:08.990
If you’re thinking it looks like something
right out of a pirate ship, you’re right.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:14.630
It is a .44 caliber single shot black powder
handgun, and it operates exactly like any

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.030
other gun of its kind.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:20.970
However, the bullet that leaves the gun does
not exit the barrel in a straight line.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:26.650
Instead, it has a target in mind as soon as
it’s been loaded, regardless of which way

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:28.950
the gun’s holder aims it.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:33.730
Once it is fired, SCP-4282 delivers a deadly
gunshot wound to the back of the head of the

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:39.130
nearest living human being guilty of piracy
or stealing a nautical ship.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:44.500
The wound is identical every time: the bullet
enters through the parietal bone and exits

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:47.130
through the right eye socket.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:51.190
This gun only comes in handy once in a blue
moon these days, since piracy has been on

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:54.590
the decline for the past couple centuries
or so, but you never know when you’ll come

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:56.550
across the old skull and crossbones.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.910
You can never be too prepared.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:04.671
Nikola Tesla was responsible for some of the
greatest technological advances in history,

00:12:04.671 --> 00:12:08.620
including the tesla coil and the remote control.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:13.370
If only he invented a way to keep me from
losing that damn thing, but I digress.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.370
Oh No!

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:15.370
What did I do!

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:21.690
One of his lesser-known inventions is SCP-2700,
which he created with the intention of producing

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:24.410
a directed-energy weapon.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:29.880
It is comprised of three parts, which, when
combined, would produce a chain reaction that

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.240
could destroy the universe as we know it.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:36.460
To explain it in layman’s terms, it would
create the opposite of the Big Bang.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:39.630
That’s one that we’d better keep under
wraps.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:41.340
Probably forever, if we can help it.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:48.600
Up next, we have SCP-2818, an array of sixteen
firearms that look identical to Barrett M82A1

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:55.640
anti-materiel rifles , with one difference:
the words “H&amp;W Mod #9” are printed on

00:12:55.640 --> 00:13:00.090
the guns where the Barrett identification
would normally be.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:06.361
These firearms load like a standard Barrett
M82A1, but if someone pulls the trigger, they

00:13:06.361 --> 00:13:07.970
will immediately disappear.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:12.990
A round will then be fired from the barrel
of the gun, but it is not the one loaded into

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.670
the gun’s chamber.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:20.540
Instead, it is comprised of the organic matter
making up the person who pulled the trigger,

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:24.740
converted into the shape of a .50 BMG round.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:28.510
These rounds match up with the estimated weight
and density of a human being that has been

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:30.930
compressed into that size and shape.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.480
It converts the soldier into the ammunition.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:36.920
Talk about human resources.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:44.810
SCP-186 was discovered in 1917, and is the
location of an unrecorded military conflict

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:49.600
between the Imperial German Army and the Russian
Provisional government.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:55.470
From this area, the SCP Foundation recovered
and contained a collection of unusual weaponry,

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.990
which are now kept in a Foundation facility.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:04.270
First, a modified version of the Skoda M1909
machine gun, which causes rapid tumorous growths

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:07.360
within the body of any organism larger than
a lab rat.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.910
There were mortar shells that contained a
gas that caused animal cells to be unable

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:11.910
to die.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:18.400
A coil of Concertina wire was discovered,
covered in an unidentifiable hallucinogenic

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.590
substance with permanent effects on the human
brain.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:25.900
Eventually, they discovered grenades filled
with a gas that is able to penetrate any gas

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:31.650
mask and cause the feeling of being lit on
fire, and a number of French rifle cartridges

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:33.460
filled with powdered human bone.

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:37.270
We’ve talked about weapons that shoot and
stab, but we haven’t yet covered one of

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:41.280
the most powerful tools of warfare: the tank.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:48.400
That brings us to SCP-802, which resembles
a World War II era Renault Char B1 medium

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.779
battle tank.

00:14:49.779 --> 00:14:54.450
Unlike other tanks from this era, which need
to be operated by a soldier inside, this tank

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:56.890
operates entirely on its own.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:15:04.940
There is no one inside running its controls,
but it still continues to operate independently.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:09.690
It has undergone severe physical damage, but
it still is plenty capable of keeping up in

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:10.690
a fight.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:14.870
It achieves a speed of up to 40 kilometers
per hour, and can take hits from anti-tank

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.730
weapons without faltering.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:21.350
It has caused over 47 casualties since being
contained, so whatever cosmetic damage it’s

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:24.360
sustained doesn’t seem to have hurt it too
much.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:28.410
Strangest of all, music plays from inside
the tank’s hull, with no apparent source.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:32.040
Usually, this music is from the late nineteenth
and early twentieth centuries.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:38.020
Though its purpose is uncertain, some researchers
believe it to be a form of psychological warfare

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:42.060
intended to unsettle the tank’s perceived
enemies.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:48.800
SCP-705 is kept in this 5 oz container of
Play-Doh, which keeps it dormant and harmless.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:53.760
If you open this container, however, the squishy
red substance inside begins to move.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:58.720
Hundreds of tiny humanoid shapes pour out
of the clay, turning into miniature army men.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.720
These aren’t your usual army man toys, though.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.930
They’re outfitted with completely functional
automatic weapons.

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:09.970
They’re also highly aggressive and territorial,
choosing locations to invade and working together

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.480
to take them over.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:16.420
They’re sentient, understand English, and
operate within a militaristic hierarchy.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:21.810
Most impressive, and troubling, of all however,
is their ability to multiply.

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.610
Get your mind out of the gutter, recruit!

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:29.730
If the tiny soldiers encounter another container
of Play-Doh, or a similar model clay, it will

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.490
also spring to life and become a new army
of tiny soldiers.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.710
Once the army’s out of the can, they will
remain active until they’ve been stuffed

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:38.020
back inside.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:41.620
You’ve probably heard of the guillotines
used to execute the powerful during the French

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:43.080
Revolution.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:50.130
SCP-374 is one of these guillotines, constructed
from an oak frame and a sharp steel blade.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:53.011
When used to execute a human being, something
bizarre happens.

00:16:53.011 --> 00:16:58.730
The head of the victim becomes overtaken by
the personality of a man from the French Revolution

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:06.010
named Jean-Philippe-Horace-Donatien for a
duration of 35 minutes.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:10.710
It is able to answer questions during this
time, though it tends to be uncooperative

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.860
due to its mistrust of the Foundation.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.980
Which, considering it becomes conscious only
after a head is chopped off a human body,

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.110
makes some sense.

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:23.430
Then we have another pistol, but one that
is like nothing else we’ve seen today.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:27.070
SCP-1998 is a pistol of unknown make and model.

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:31.440
The peculiar thing about 1998 is its lack
of any ammunition.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:36.000
Rather than firing any kind of bullets, the
gun fires a pulse of energy from an undetermined

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.480
power source.

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:41.340
These pulses of energy have no effect on a
target that is not a human body.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:46.750
If it hits a human, however, it has a notable
effect on the brain, particularly the motor

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:51.350
cortex, the primary auditory cortex, and the
hippocampus.

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:53.970
Once someone has been hit, three things happen.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:58.550
First, the target turns and sits down in front
of the person wielding SCP-1998.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:03.430
Then, the target becomes paralyzed and has
no control over their physical movement.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:09.690
The target will then listen to, and believe,
anything that the person firing SCP-1998 says

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:10.690
to them.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:14.059
The operator of the weapon is then able to
rewrite their victim’s memories and give

00:18:14.059 --> 00:18:19.210
them commands, which the victim will follow
as closely as possible as soon as they can

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.650
move again.

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:25.429
Victims of SCP-1998 have described the effects
of the weapon as horrifically painful and

00:18:25.429 --> 00:18:28.800
traumatic, and that comes as no surprise.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:34.400
It is, essentially, a weapon that allows its
user to fight against free will itself.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.520
Now get to work!

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:40.960
And remember, as you walk past the containment
cells, keep your eyes to yourself.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:46.230
You might see something you don’t want to
see…or something that really, really doesn’t

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:49.000
want you to see it.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:55.050
Now go check out “SCP-3108 The Nerfing Gun”
and “SCP Elite Mobile Task Force Explained”

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:58.019
for more combat and weaponry at the SCP Foundation.

